ame conclusion holds under the alternative condition $\\delta(G) \\ge \\sqrt{n}$δ(G)≥n​. In this paper, we construct counterexamples that completely disprove the first conjecture. Furthermore, using the existence of $(v, k, 2)$(v,k,2)-Symmetric Balanced Incomplete Block designs (i.e., SBIBDs), we disprove the second conjecture for all $n \\in \\{8, 14, 22, 32, 74, 112, 158\\}$n∈{8,14,22,32,74,112,158}. Finally, we propose a conjecture of our own: for any $2$2-connected graph $G$G on $n$n vertices with $\\delta(G) \\ge \\frac{n}{k}$δ(G)≥k n​, where $k \\ge 3$k≥3 and $n$n is sufficiently large, $G$G contains a $2$2-connected subgraph of every order from $4$4 to $n$n.\n\n### Keywords\n\nhadwiger conjecture graph connectivity graph theory\n\n### Cite\n    \n    @article{arxiv.2603.11662,\n      title  = {An Improved Interpolation Theorem and Disproofs of Two Conjectures on 2-Connected Subgraphs},\n      author = {Haiyang Liu and Bo Ning},\n      journal= {arXiv preprint arXiv:2603.11662},\n      year   = {2026}\n    }\n\n### Comments\n\n11 pages\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the sum of k largest singular values of graphs and matrices (https://arxiv.org/abs/1007.3949)\nciteturn0academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 16.3 years ago; Authors: Vladimir Nikiforov ... In the recent years, the trace norm of graphs has been extensively studied under the name of graph energy. The trace norm is just one of the Ky Fan k-norms, given by the sum of the k largest singular values, which are studied more generally in the present paper.\nTitle: On the sum of k largest singular values of graphs and matrices\nAuthors: Vladimir Nikiforov\nDate: Thu Jul 22 17:26:37 2010\n\nIn the recent years, the trace norm of graphs has been extensively studied under the name of graph energy. The trace norm is just one of the Ky Fan k-norms, given by the sum of the k largest singular values, which are studied more generally in the present paper. Sev